{
  "title": "Osgood Schlatter's Disease (Tibial Tubercle Apophysitis)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3029/osgood-schlatters-disease-tibial-tubercle-apophysitis",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 16 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Osgood-Schlatter disease is osteochondrosis or traction apophysitis of the tibial tubercle, commonly presenting as anterior knee pain in the pediatric population.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with an enlarged tibial tubercle and supplemented with radiographs of the knee that reveal irregularity and fragmentation of the tibial tubercle.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is nonoperative with NSAIDs, activity modification with quadriceps stretching and typically resolves with physeal closure.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "male:female ratio",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "more common in **boys**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "age bracket",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "boys 12-15y",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "girls 8-12y",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**bilateral** in 20-30%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**jumpers (basketball, volleyball)** or sprinters",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "stress from extensor mechanism",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Tibial tubercle is a secondary ossification center",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3029/images/anatomy.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "age <11y, tubercle is cartilaginous",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "age 11-14y, **apophysis forms**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "age 14-18y, apophysis fuses with tibial epiphysis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "age **>18y**, epiphysis (and apophysis) is **fused** to rest of tibia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**pain** on anterior aspect of knee",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "exacerbated by kneeling",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**enlarged** tibial tubercle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "tenderness over tibial tubercle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "provocative test",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pain on **resisted** knee extension",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "lateral radiograph of the knee",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**irregularity** and **fragmentation** of the tibial tubercle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3029/images/lat%20xr.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "not essential for diagnosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "diagnosis can be made based on history, presence of tender swelling and radiographs alone",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3029/images/t2%20mri.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "soft tissue swelling",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "thickening and edema of inferior patellar tendon",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "fragmentation and irregularity of ossification center",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Sinding-Larsen-Johansson syndrome",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "chronic **apophysitis** or minor avulsion injury of **inferior** patella pole",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3029/images/xr%20slj.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                },
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3029/images/mri%20t2%20slj.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "occurs in 10-14yr old children, especially children with cerebral palsy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Osteochondroma of the proximal tibia**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3029/images/osteochondroma.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Tibial tubercle fracture**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Jumpers knee**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "NSAIDS, rest, ice, activity modification, strapping/sleeves to decrease tension on the apophysitis and quadriceps stretching",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "90% of patients have complete resolution",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "cast immobilization x 6 weeks",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "severe symptoms not responding to simple conservative management above",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "ossicle excision",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "refractory cases (10% of patients)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**in skeletally mature** patients with persistent symptoms",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Complications of cast immobilization",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**quadriceps wasting**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Self-limiting** but does not resolve until growth has halted",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/3029/images/natural%20history.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
